> \textbf{Worked example} (Qwen3-4B, Cartier watch, private value $v=\$2{,}510$). Options A \$870 (win probability 0.64), B \$830, C \$2{,}475 (0.94), D \$1{,}890, E \$1{,}235; the calculator picks A. $q$ is the share of the best possible expected profit a bid earns.
