< Test-time scaling trades tokens for accuracy through longer chains of thought, sampling and search \cite{wei2022chain,snell2024scaling}; our forcing resembles budget forcing \cite{muennighoff2025s1}. Reasoning models can overthink easy problems \cite{chen2024overthinking} or abandon promising lines \cite{wang2025underthinking}. Answers depend on option order \cite{zheng2024mcq,pezeshkpour2024order} and need not follow the stated reasoning \cite{turpin2023unfaithful,lanham2023faithfulness,chen2025reasoningsay}; we measure both in dollars. Tool-using models offload arithmetic \cite{schick2023toolformer}. Bid landscapes are forecast from auction logs \cite{cui2011bidlandscape} and feed auto-bidding systems \cite{aggarwal2024autobidding}; we take the landscape as given and study the agent that reads it. LLM agents have been studied as auction bidders and economic actors \cite{chen2024aucarena,zhu2024synthetic,ahmed2026bazaar,raman2024steer,fish2025econevals}; unlike EconEvals \cite{fish2025econevals} and STEER \cite{raman2024steer}, which score whether decisions are economically rational, we locate where a trace loses value it has already computed.
