> \paragraph{Overview}
> Forcing 768 tokens recovers 42--85\% of the calculator's lead (Table~\ref{tab:main}), almost all of it above 256 tokens; in dollars pooled over decisions, where Cartier weighs most, it recovers 25--75\%. Arithmetic is a small share of what remains for five models: at most 5\% of the gap with the lower bound and 17\% with the upper (Table~\ref{tab:traces}). For every model most of the loss comes after the best option's value is on the page. Shares move by at most 11 points at match tolerances of 1--5\% or under FP eq., and FP eq.\ recovery varies by at most 4 points across value distribution, bid increment and number of bidders (README).
