< \paragraph{Truncation and decision.}
< Following traces as they grow separates two failures, since greedy forced traces at 512 tokens are prefixes of those at 768. When a trace that was unfinished at 512 tokens, with the best option ranked first, finishes its list by 768, DeepSeek-8B and the Qwen models answer correctly in 84--89\% of cases, Phi-mini and Granite-8B in 52\% and 46\%. Unforced traces agree: once the list is finished, Phi-mini and Granite-8B still pass over the trace's own best option in 50\% and 40\% of cases, the others in under 10\%. For the Qwen models, then, most of the loss is the budget, as the 4{,}096-token run confirms; for Phi-mini and Granite-8B the answer fails after the reasoning is done.
