< \paragraph{The readout.}
< Is the letter the model's real answer? A rule-based parser reads the last answer the trace itself states (``the highest expected profit is Option C''). Where it fires, it agrees with the letter in 96--98\% of Qwen traces and 93\% of Granite-8B's finished traces, but in only 57\% of Phi-mini's. Phi-mini's stated choice is the best option in 94\% of those decisions, its letter in 55\%; of the 156 passed-over letters whose trace states a choice, 139 state the best option. Taking the stated answer where there is one raises Phi-mini's recovery from 42\% to 64\% [56, 71]. Phi-mini's passing over is therefore mostly a readout failure, while Granite-8B's own words pass over the best option too.
