> \paragraph{Decision and arithmetic: Granite-8B}
> Granite-8B's loss is split between arithmetic and passing over, and the split is uncertain. With the lower bound, 22\% of its gap is arithmetic and 61\% passed over; with the upper bound, 45\% and 37\%. Its own stated answer agrees with its letter in 93\% of finished traces, so the passing over is not a readout effect. When its list finishes between 512 and 768 tokens it answers correctly in only 46\% of cases, and moving the best option from first to last cuts the odds of passing it over to 0.15.
